## What the actual tests establish

The new ordinary fixture has a real generated World, Nodes, Directory,
Resident/Transform, Inventory, Pool, Work/Gear, Construction, Sites, Router,
SpaceOwner, Locations, WorldRoutes/Routes and original structural reader. It
loads immutable source wires unchanged. Its pre-existing Corridor identity
and physical bootstrap are named fixture boundaries; no paid Site bytes or
cut history are seeded.

The complete published FRONT16/rev1 source locally clears its actual solid
target through WorkFace. Tests retain real geometry when the published WALK
cannot reach it. Binding/reentry/original weak reference failures preserve
unbound state and permit corrected retry. Profile/Catalog publication,
foreign replacements, Location restore, selector publication without a Space
revision and overflow all invalidate cached qualification. Two genuinely
WorkFace-qualified alternatives do not make an actual assigned worker's
committed endpoint/profile ambiguous. Worker-free selection remains unique.
All-living-resident physical registration is explicit and exercised with an
actual remote unregistered Resident, removal and retry.

The optional Entry Contacts lifetime is distinct from a never-bound ordinary
composition. An existing WeakRef whose actual receiver expires keeps
qualification unavailable. The targeted refusal-only injected fault checks a
real RefCounted lifetime transition, repeated refusal, unchanged original
packet identities, paid/physical state, lease counters and publication tokens.
The correction introduces no allocation site or new member. These logical
checks are not transient native-allocation measurement.

Existing Entry fixture reuse proves that the new subclass does not grant an
unbound Entry contact permission, and preserves real original BRACE START,
Work, payment and settlement. Its source geometry/certificates remain the
historical explicitly synthetic fixture. The FINISH adaptation tests use real
BRACE/CUT/FINISH paid state from the accepted phase-refresh fixture, including
released-worker terminal scope, but retain that fixture's synthetic physical
companion. These remain separately scoped component regressions, distinct from
the actual geometry/payment sequence below.

## Actual first-cube diagnostic

The copied `approach-profile-diagnostic-1/` input is the root-authored v3 wire
`a581f90aa0db07187a1dfc1f0836bd7f3de39d401ff944db07a3958649b1c204`:
wire2/content2, row revision1, 26 profiles and 250 boxes. The immutable source
report, serializer manifest and copied-input hashes are retained. Its fixture
certificate15 does not establish native/production/world qualification.

| Role | World XYZ u | Explicit source |
|---|---|---|
| Work station | (124160, -4608, 102912) | FRONT24/rev1, body yaw49152 |
| Target cube origin | (124928, -4608, 102400) | exact -X face |
| Access, storage and retreat | (121856, -4608, 102912) | one full STORAGE endpoint |
| Approach | access → work | row5, path/body yaw49152 |
| Retreat | work → access | row9, body49152 / path16384 |

Actual WorldRoutes proves both authored directed paths. Actual RoomOrders
confirms a 2×2 Kitchen, then the real assigned worker walks in, enters the
canonical WORK source phase, pays and completes BRACE, CUT and FINISH through
Sites/Funding/Inventory/Work and original sealed companions. Canonical recovery
finishes before each Job/tool release. The actual backwards source returns
the worker to the original endpoint after terminal settlement. No productive
credit is earned by walking, entry, recovery or settlement retry.

The complete first cube consumes **250 milli wood and 250 milli stone**, earns
exactly **9,000 mWU**, and emits **2,000 milli earth**. Support/earth conservation,
one retained cut-history row, no remaining phase Project and original Budget
quiescence are asserted. The other claimed Kitchen cubes remain unpaid.
Materials are finite real Inventory stock; delivery-source activation is not
claimed by this fixture.

All nine non-contact source boxes remain exact Plan volumes. The three complete
BODY/TURN/APPROACH floor residuals remain at Y[-1,0), with their full source and
WorkFace proof; only source primitives with actual above-plane air produce
approach rows. No negative geometry is clipped or granted a support exception.
A direct mutation regression rejects a changed residual. Readiness uses observed
`source_work_observation_refusal`, then the concrete static final leaf and
decoded `actor_phase_in`; no raw source phase bits or render-ready authority.

The final START adversary moves the real worker after successful observations:
payment, WIP, Work/XP/wear and Space remain unchanged; restoring that deliberate
negative mutation permits the original unpaid phase to retry once. The terminal
CUT adversary changes the borrowed context's full Site after observations;
output and topology refuse, then the completed phase retries after its worker
and tool claim are already released, without extra WU or duplicated earth.

The old published v2 WALK refusal remains tested and unchanged. The v3 API and
certificate are diagnostic prerequisites until1156 native/source integration
is independently accepted. No source guard, budget or production artifact is
relaxed here.

